# Docs structure

Follow the Vercel AI SDK docs pattern: folders are categories; the folder index is the category page, not a sidebar child.

## Frontmatter

Every MDX page needs:

```yaml
---
title: Short title
description: One promise. What the reader can do after this page.
---
```

## Trees

| Tree | Use for |
|---|---|
| `content/docs/concepts/` | How the SDK works (client, tools, schema, mock, retries) |
| `content/docs/providers/` | Provider-specific setup and examples |
| `content/docs/api/` | Object/API reference |
| `content/docs/` root | Introduction (`index.mdx`), getting-started |
| `content/learn/` | Tutorials, narrative guides, changelog |

## Navigation (AI SDK style)

- Nest folders with `"concepts"`, `"providers"`, `"api"` in the parent `pages` array. Do **not** use `"...concepts"` (that **extracts**/flattens children into the parent).
- Do **not** list `"index"` in a folder's `pages` array. `index.mdx` is the folder index (clickable folder name). Listing it turns it into a duplicate child.
- Folder `meta.json` `title` and `index.mdx` `title` should match the category (e.g. both `Concepts`).
- Avoid `---Section---` separators that repeat a folder or page name next to that folder/page.
- Keep page order teachable: introduction, getting started, then concept/provider/API folders.

```json
// content/docs/meta.json
{
  "pages": ["index", "getting-started", "concepts", "providers", "api"]
}

// content/docs/concepts/meta.json
{
  "title": "Concepts",
  "pages": ["client", "structured-output", "tools", "mock", "retries"]
}

// content/docs/concepts/index.mdx
title: Concepts
```

Sidebar result: **Introduction**, **Getting Started**, **Concepts** (folder → index) with Client/Tools/… as children. No "Concepts / Concepts".

## Cross-links

Link concepts, API, and providers instead of repeating the same deep explanation on every page.
